  "worked_solution": "The difference $T\u2216S$ consists of all the elements that are in $T$ but not $S.$ To represent $T\u2216S,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $T$ but not $S.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/c718918667c5076f8696ea98f453ff17f005d5f7cace87bd863be309fac28d72.png)\n\nThe elements $t,e,$ and $l$ are in $T$ but not $S.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nT\u2216S={t,e,l}.\n$$",
